    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on August 22, the lineup hinges on a favorable park factor and platoon alignment for our infield power core. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.26) represent our strongest plays of the day. Despite facing a tough arm in McClanahan, both benefit from a significant +16% park factor adjustment, and **Coby Mayo** specifically capitalizes on a favorable platoon edge (+8%) that elevates his ceiling. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) remains a pillar of the offense; even with a challenging matchup against Weathers, his ability to leverage the dynamic platoon (+7%) and a prime #2 spot in the order ensures he stays in the elite tier of our daily projections.\n\nThe optimization process faced a tight margin regarding the final UTIL and OF slots, with **Miguel Vargas** (45.54) ultimately squeezing into the lineup over available bench depth. While **Miguel Vargas** projects as a marginal start, his high xwOBA (0.382) provides a safer floor compared to the volatility of our other depth pieces. We are closely monitoring the status of our injured reserve\u2014**Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Josh Jung** remain sidelined\u2014leaving our bench shallow. Should we need to pivot, reserves such as **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, or **Tommy White** would be forced into action, though none currently match the projected efficiency of the starters.\n\nRisk mitigation is the priority today, particularly regarding stolen base opportunities. While **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) is a strong play, we are wary of his \"Elite Hold SP\" tag, which marginally dampens his projected efficiency despite his 40% SB contribution. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Heliot Ramos** (45.34); while his base score is lower, he benefits from a +2% bump due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which may provide the opportunistic SB chance we need to bolster our scarcest category. Managers should monitor weather updates for the late-afternoon slate, but for now, the data suggests leaning into the power of **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson** to anchor our Roto performance.",
